        "evidence": "The chart shows TX as pale yellow (high risk) and DE as orange-red (moderate risk). TX is visually higher risk than DE. However, the chart also shows other states like MT, OR, NV, UT, FL, and WA that are also pale yellow or light yellow, indicating they are at or near the same high-risk level as TX. The routing criterion is 'Highest risk state in the dashboard', which is not restricted to the offered options. Therefore, TX is not necessarily the only or the highest-risk state; multiple states are at the highest level. The B reading correctly states that selection is only valid if the offered state exceeds every other mapped state, which is not the case for TX or DE. RI is gray and has no assigned risk value, so it is ineligible for comparison under this B condition. Therefore, the B reading is not satisfied for any of the offered states under this interpretation.",
