        "evidence": "The offered options are RI, NM, and DE. RI is gray and has no assigned risk value, so it is ineligible for comparison. NM is dark burgundy-red, which is the lowest risk color shown (near 0). DE is orange-red, which is moderate risk. The chart shows that NM is at the lowest risk level, while DE is at a moderate level. Therefore, under this B reading, DE is the highest-risk among the offered options. The B reading correctly states that the offered state with the highest legend-decoded risk is the most consistent choice, and DE is that state. The B reading is supported by the visible evidence.",
